%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: 7000Steps
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261442
    - rid: 4351267832094261443
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: -so are we actually climbing 7000 steps?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261444
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Technically no, I don't remember how many steps there are exactly, just
      that there are less than 7000.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261445
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Then why are they called that?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261446
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Because lore-wise they actually are 7000 steps, but that sort of scale
      couldn't be replicated in-game.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261447
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Does that happen often?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261448
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Often?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Only across <i>every single physical location</i>, yeah.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: If you keep acting snippy, I'll make you carry me.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261449
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: And take away your chances to be the first 18 year-old girl to climb
      the 7000 steps?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261451
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Perish the thought!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261450
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Monika and {mc} spot Klimmek, who has packed supplies for the Graybeards.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261452
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: '{mc} offers to take them up, since he''s climbing the mountain anyway.'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Grateful for the help, Klimmek hands over the supplies and walks back
      toward Ivarstead.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261453
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: 'You know, Natsuki said you were a: "good boy."'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261454
    - rid: 4351267832094261455
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: ... what?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Funny, that's exactly what I said too!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261456
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: ... what'd she mean by that?!?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Surprisingly, nothing much.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261457
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Just that she thinks you are a boy who is good.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261458
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: No hidden layers; nothing.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261459
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ?!?!?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: And why are you telling me this?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh come on, you were <i>trying</i> to be all boring and keeping to yourself
      on the way to Ivarstead.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261460
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I gotta fill up these less-than-7000 steps with something.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261461
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... women.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Can we talk about literally anything else?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261462
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Coward.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm fine with being called a coward if it means we don't have to partake
      in your putrid gossip.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Putrid?!?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261463
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: '{mc}, I''ll have you know the girls would <i>kill</i> for the kind of
      gossip I wield.'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: And <i>I would kill</i> to never have to bear witness to the gossip you
      wield.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Party pooper.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261464
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261465
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Whatever. You said that the Graybeards aren't dragonborn?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261466
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: That is correct; they are not.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: So how can they speak the dragon language, or Thu'um, or however you
      put it?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, there's technically a history lesson there.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ... fine.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261467
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Lay it on me, {mc}.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267832094261468
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Alright, so back when the dragons ruled Skyrim...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093171
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: The Nords would often pray to their gods, seeking relief from the yoke
      of the dragon.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So, their goddess of nature, Kyne-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Kyne? Is she related to Kynareth, the god that Sayori's "master" supposedly
      works for?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093172
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Actually, yes!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093173
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Kyne is the Nordic name for the Imperial/Aldmeri deity Kynareth.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Most of the major religions in Tamriel, especially in present-day, are
      essentially variations on the same eight divines-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: With different names, and sometimes different dieties included.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, Kyne decided to be a pal, and told a traitorous dragon named
      Paarthurnax to teach men how to use the Thu'um.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Actually, Paarthurnax is still alive to this day and is the Graybeards'
      master.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh, are we going to meet him?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093174
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Not today, no. He perches himself up at the peak of the mountain, which
      is particularly secluded.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093175
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Also, he's voiced by Mario.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ... what?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093176
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: In the game, he's voiced by Charles Martinet, who's the English voice
      actor for Mario-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093177
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Ah crap...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093178
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Uh, {mc}, why'd you stop-?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093179
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Monika's question is quickly answered, as the notorious frost troll descends
      from his ledge.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093180
    - rid: 4351267851529093181
    - rid: 4351267851529093182
    - rid: 4351267851529093201
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093183
    - rid: 4351267851529093184
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: The hell was that, {mc}!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093200
    - rid: 4351267851529093202
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: That was a frost troll, perhaps the most infamous one at that.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093203
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: The most infamous one?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093206
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah, when people first play Skyrim, they often just go along with the
      main quest at the start-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093207
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: When they encounter that frost troll, who's always perched up on <i>that</i>
      ledge and is stronger than most characters by that time of the game.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: A lot of saves are reloaded right here...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: But we won, so it's fine.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093208
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I see...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093209
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093210
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093212
    - rid: 4351267851529093213
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: The air's getting a little bit thin up here...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093214
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: You're not wrong...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: But! We're almost there, so we don't need to push much further.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093215
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093216
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh, is that it?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267851529093217
